Count REP string iterations against the step budget

The x86 sandbox limits each call to a number of executed instructions, and
tiny386 counted a REP string instruction as one instruction however many
iterations it ran. Each iteration now counts, in cpu->cycle and in
cpu_exec1's step count. When the step count runs out with iterations left,
the instruction stops with its registers updated so far and runs again at the
next step.

